{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>He opened, [and] waters</b> — [it is] hof'al [passive], used a second time, as in <i>'ונבואה עודד הנביא'</i> (II Chronicles 15:8). Likewise, <i>הלכו בציון</i> ['they walked in Zion'] is plural form, from <i>ציה</i> ['dry land']; [compare] <i>מי נהר</i> ['waters of a river']."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {0 "The three scriptural phrases quoted are in Hebrew script in the original. 'Used a second time' likely means this hof'al root recurs elsewhere; the reference to II Chronicles 15:8 (where the same rare hof'al of פתח appears) is inferred. The last two examples illustrate singular nouns used in construct or plural-like forms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:37.157145884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}